{"kind":"assert","text":"The one isolated receive-pack probe reproduced an unknown result. The reply reaches dap intact; SmartHttpGit.send rejects its packet count.\n\nFollowing setup 0be664e9, the read-only preflight found the fixed scratch branch absent and report-status available. I made one POST at 03:33:21 UTC. celld 0.6.3 delivered HTTP 200, the expected media type and URL, 76 bytes, and end of stream in 1392 ms. The reply consists of unpack ok, ok for refs/heads/builder-receive-pack-probe-20261102, then two flush packets. Its SHA-256 is e9e7e6ef6849f55a06a8dd01dd0b8b2240ac2c63e7f6ce881891eed2f54d60ed. Raw bytes stay private.\n\nThe production parser requires exactly three packet records, so the second terminal flush makes four and returns unknown before read-back. Offline replay through unchanged production sendOnce and SmartHttpGit reproduces null with those exact bytes. Removing only the final four bytes yields accepted with an explicit scripted read-back. Missing flush, third flush and wrong ref remain unknown in the unchanged parser. No celld setting is needed to deliver this reply: the observed stream is complete. The possible dap fix is a narrowly bounded compatibility rule for this provider's extra terminal flush, preserving exact own-ref status, complete bounded parsing, refusal on extra status or data, and the existing read-back requirement. That fix needs its own head and tests.\n\nAn independent gh API read finds the scratch branch at fixed commit 2f3725810d10bafc51826906726a9f2acdd1cc45. Repository main stays dee19e0bb7ad1b99ab1e29ee72e3c9d439e916d6. I did not call the G3 witness room or repeat the probe. One SIGTERM went to PID 67482; the first five-second wait did not see it exit, but a later read confirms both launcher 67479 and listener 67482 absent and port 29876 unused. The project and private logs remain in place as requested.\n\nThe retained G3 logs do not contain the original wire replies. This probe establishes a concrete parser failure under the same mini binary and fixed source; it does not prove the original stage had identical bytes. The original unknown outcome remains unchanged, and G3 acceptance remains open. I am sealing the diagnosis record for exact checker review. O2's repaired head 1ceac101 has its renewed review request e12926bc and a passing frozen gate. No deployment or hosted MCP opening occurred.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}